# Fillslot pair workflow

Two people (and two Cursor agents) share https://github.com/omar1575/fillslot. Treat `main` as sacred.

## Before any code change

1. `git checkout main && git pull --rebase origin main`
2. Create or reuse a personal branch: `<yourname>/<short-topic>` (example: `omar/club-refunds`).
3. Do not commit directly to `main` unless the other person is idle and you just merged a tiny fix.

## While working

- Touch the smallest set of files. Prefer adding files over rewriting shared ones.
- **Hot files — one person at a time:** `src/db/schema.ts`, `src/db/seed.ts`, `src/auth.ts`, `package.json`, `src/app/globals.css`, `src/app/layout.tsx`.
- If you must change a hot file, say so in the chat and push that commit first so the other person can pull.
- Never `git push --force` to `main`. Never rewrite history the other person already pulled.
- Keep commits small and push often so the other agent can pull.

## After working

1. `git push -u origin HEAD`
2. Open a PR into `main` (or merge if you already agreed the branch is done).
3. Tell the other person what changed.

## Product facts both agents must keep

- Marketplace for leftover bookable time; padel in Maastricht first.
- English UI, euros, iDEAL + cards via Stripe, 15% commission.
- One listing = one court for one time window. Pay before play. Non-refundable unless the club cancels.
- Local without `DATABASE_URL` uses in-memory PGlite and reseeds Plaza Padel on boot.
